<title>UK: Turkey sets 500 million mark seven-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>Turkey sets 500 million mark seven-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Commerzbank and Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
<p> BORROWER   TURKEY</p>
<p> AMT    500 MLN DEM   COUPON     7.75	MATURITY    17.FEB.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.90     PAY DATE    17.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.75	REOFFER    98.40     SPREAD	+275 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	BB3	 LISTING    FRANKFURT PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  B	   DENOMS (K) 1	   SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.75	SELL CONC  1.50	LISTING FEE 0.50</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND NOV 2003 TREUHAND</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
